course: dictionary
lesson: 5043
title: Words for place
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Inland means in or towards the middle of a country, away from the coast or the sea. The word is built from in and land, so it tells you the place is inside the land, not on its edge.
explain: «If an earthquake at the coast is long or strong, go to high ground or inland at once.» The coast is the edge where land meets the sea, so inland is the opposite: the land further away from the water. Inland can also be an adjective, as in «an inland town», or an adverb, as in «travel inland».
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «Far inland» could mean a long way from the sea. If you put that in the sentence, does it still make sense? It does, so you have found the meaning.
fact: Inland means away from the coast or the sea.
fact: «Inland» can be an adjective, as in «an inland town», or an adverb, as in «travel inland».
fact: «Move inland» means go away from the sea, to land further from the coast, especially in a tsunami warning.
fact: Inland places often have hotter summers and colder winters than the coast, because the sea keeps coastal weather milder.
fact: Lake Superior is a huge inland lake, and much of inland Australia is the dry Outback.
exercise: «If an earthquake at the coast is long or strong, go to high ground or inland at once.» What does inland mean here? | Right on the beach | Under the ground in a cave | Out at sea, on the water | *Away from the coast, further into the land
exercise: Which place is inland? | *A town 300 km from the coast | A rock pool on the beach | A boat out on the ocean | A ferry crossing the sea
exercise: «The wave floods far inland, like the whole sea climbing onto the land.» What does far inland mean? | Along the edge of the cliffs | Under the sea | Very close to the waves | *A long way from the sea, deep into the land
test: Which word means away from the sea? | Coastal | *Inland | Tidal | Offshore
test: Why do inland places often have hotter summers and colder winters than the coast? | Because the coast has more sunshine | *Because the sea keeps coastal weather milder | Because inland towns have more rain | Because inland places are always higher up
exam: In «Long or strong, get gone», what should you do if the shaking is long or strong? | Stay indoors and close the windows | Go down to the beach to look at the waves | *Go to high ground or inland at once | Wait for a siren before you move
